      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes the Rust-frontend half of #58144.\n\n`GUARDED_PREFIXES` only matched `/v1`, `/v2` and `/inference`, so any route outside those prefixes was reachable without a bearer token even when `--api-key` was configured. This includes `/tokenize`, `/detokenize`, `/metrics`, `/reset_prefix_cache`, `/reset_mm_cache`, `/reset_encoder_cache`, `/collective_rpc`, `/update_weights`, `/abort_requests`, `/sleep`, `/wake_up`, `/pause`, `/resume`, `/server_info`, `/get_world_size`, and `/start_profile`/`/stop_profile`.\n\nThis mirrors the same allowlist-of-guarded-prefixes defect that #58028 fixes on the Python frontend for the same issue. As noted in a comment on #58144: \"The Rust frontend has the same bug ... `--api-key` behaves differently per frontend.\" This PR closes that gap on the Rust side.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace `GUARDED_PREFIXES` (allowlist of what's guarded, fails open on new routes) with `UNGUARDED_PATHS` (allowlist of what's exempt — `/health`, `/load`, `/version`), so every route, present or added later, requires a token by default.\n\n## Duplicate-work check\n\n- `gh issue view 58144 --repo vllm-project/vllm --comments`\n- `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search \"58144 in:body\"` → #58028 (Python side, still open) and #58341 (narrower `/invocations`-only patch) address the Python frontend; neither touches `rust/src/server/src/middleware/auth.rs`. This PR is scoped to the Rust frontend only, which a comment on #58144 explicitly flagged as unaddressed.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `cargo test -p vllm-server`\n- `cargo fmt -p vllm-server -- --check`\n- `cargo clippy -p vllm-server --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n\n## Test Result\n\n- `cargo test -p vllm-server`: 429 passed, 0 failed (includes 2 new regression tests proving `/tokenize` and `/metrics` now require a token, and that OPTIONS/CORS-preflight/guarded/unguarded behavior is unchanged)\n- `cargo fmt -- --check`: clean\n- `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`: clean\n\nAI assistance was used (Claude Code) to draft and test this change; I reviewed every changed line and ran the commands above myself.",
